Summary
The Floyd-Warshall algorithm is a dynamic programming algorithm used to find the shortest paths between all pairs of vertices in a weighted graph. It considers every vertex as an intermediate vertex and updates the distance matrix to obtain the shortest distances.

Conclusion
Thus, the Floyd-Warshall algorithm was successfully implemented in Python to find the shortest paths between all pairs of vertices in a weighted graph. The shortest distance matrix was displayed along with its time and space complexities.
